'' String lowering against the ABI measured in docs/internals/phase-6-rtl.md: a
'' var-length string is passed as a POINTER TO ITS DESCRIPTOR with a length of -1.
''
'' 'a = a + b' is a CONCAT-ASSIGN rather than a concat plus a store, which is what fbc
'' emits: the destination is also the left operand, so no temporary is needed. A
'' general 'a = b + c' does need one and is deliberately not lowered yet.
''
'' fb_StrDelete goes through the cleanup list, so it inherits the order measured from
'' fbc: reverse declaration, and every open scope on an early RETURN.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/mir/src/strings.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: local agg a size 24
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_StrAssign(@a, -1, @b, -1, 0)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl ptr fb_StrConcatAssign(@a, -1, @b, -1, 0)
'' EXPECT-OUT: call.rtl void fb_StrDelete(@a)
'' EXPECT-OUT: verify: ok
'' GOLDEN: expected/strings.out
